  "notes": [
    "Bi-encoder prefixes: query='', document=''. Score = cosine similarity. Member embeddings are precomputed once per evaluation (and once before latency timing).",
    "Loss: MultipleNegativesRankingLoss (scale 20) over the positive, its hard/random negatives and in-batch candidates; in-batch candidates that are themselves relevant to the anchor task are masked out (only 48 distinct profiles exist, so collisions are frequent). In-batch negatives come from the per-device micro-batch.",
    "Every Task_Assignment pair has Plausibility > 0, so no over-qualified pair has relevance 0. The task's most over-qualified present member (largest Capability - Plausibility, gap >= overqualified_min_gap) is added as an extra negative for the task's top positive only.",
    "Training tuples (anchor, positive, negatives): 19546 from 5000 tasks.",
    "train_time_s covers the fit loop including the per-epoch validation passes.",
    "Mid-unit resume: a resume checkpoint is written every 15 min and at each epoch boundary; an interrupted unit continues from it (same data order and RNG state)."
  ],
